  "seven_q": {
    "Q0_posture": "Declared position: author believes in God and that math and divine truth are dual projections, but argues this paper stands on logic alone, not theology.",
    "Q1_identity": "A foundational philosophical paper arguing for the ontological priority of mathematical structure over physical reality.",
    "Q2_domain": "Primarily philosophy of mathematics and physics, with implications for theology.",
    "Q3_claim": "Mathematical structure is ontologically prior to physical reality; math came first, matter came second.",
    "Q4_support": "Seven-property comparison table, 13.8 billion year temporal gap, Wigner's unreasonable effectiveness, five limitation theorems (G\u00f6del, Tarski, Turing, Second Law, Landauer), and falsification criteria.",
    "Q5_dependencies": "Assumes the validity of the five limitation theorems, the empirical fact of mathematical law in the early universe, and the standard definitions of necessity, eternity, immutability, and universality.",
    "Q6_consequences": "If true, nominalism, Platonism, and fictionalism are all inadequate; physics is grounded in mathematics; the universe is fundamentally mathematical; and the question of what grounds mathematics itself becomes pressing.",
    "Q7_kill": "Produce a contingent mathematical truth, a temporal mathematical truth, a local mathematical truth, explain causal efficacy of abstract objects without agency, or provide an alternative explanation for Wigner's effectiveness that does not presuppose ontological priority."
  },
